{"id":"sc900_p1_q031","exam":"SC-900","domain":"security_compliance_identity","objective":"security_compliance_concepts","subobjective":"defense in depth","difficulty":"beginner","type":"multiple_choice","stem":"Why does a defense-in-depth strategy use multiple layers of security controls?","choices":[{"id":"a","text":"To guarantee that all data stays in one country"},{"id":"b","text":"To eliminate the need for identity controls"},{"id":"c","text":"So that failure or bypass of one layer does not leave the system entirely unprotected"},{"id":"d","text":"To replace monitoring with preventive controls only"}],"correct_answer":"c","explanation":"Defense in depth uses multiple complementary layers so that a single control failure does not result in complete loss of protection.","references":["https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-security-concepts-methodologies/"],"tags":["defense in depth","defense_in_depth"],"source":{"title":"Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-security-concepts-methodologies/"},"metadata":{"origin":"manual","batch":"phase1-batch-04","blueprint_leaf_id":"defense_in_depth","source_authority":"microsoft_learn","source_urls":["https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-security-concepts-methodologies/"],"source_retrieved_at":"2026-09-11","source_family_id":"learn-security_compliance_concepts","semantic_family_id":"defense_in_depth","stem_style":"direct_concept","future_probe_suitability":"eligible","authoring_origin":"original_from_official_source"}}
{"id":"sc900_p1_q032","exam":"SC-900","domain":"microsoft_entra","objective":"entra_identity_types_and_function","subobjective":"identity types including agent id","difficulty":"beginner","type":"multiple_choice","stem":"Which Microsoft Entra capability area includes identities used by people, workloads, external users, and AI agents?","choices":[{"id":"a","text":"Azure DDoS Protection"},{"id":"b","text":"Microsoft Purview retention"},{"id":"c","text":"Microsoft Sentinel incidents"},{"id":"d","text":"Microsoft Entra ID identity types"}],"correct_answer":"d","explanation":"Microsoft Entra ID supports multiple identity types, including human, workload, external, and agent identities used by AI scenarios.","references":["https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/explore-basic-services-identity-types/"],"tags":["identity types","agent id","identity_types_including_agent_id"],"source":{"title":"Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/explore-basic-services-identity-types/"},"metadata":{"origin":"manual","batch":"phase1-batch-04","blueprint_leaf_id":"identity_types_including_agent_id","source_authority":"microsoft_learn","source_urls":["https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/explore-basic-services-identity-types/"],"source_retrieved_at":"2026-09-11","source_family_id":"learn-entra_identity_types_and_function","semantic_family_id":"identity_types_including_agent_id","stem_style":"distinction_comparison","future_probe_suitability":"eligible","authoring_origin":"original_from_official_source"}}
{"id":"sc900_p1_q033","exam":"SC-900","domain":"microsoft_entra","objective":"entra_access_management","subobjective":"conditional access","difficulty":"beginner","type":"multiple_choice","stem":"A Conditional Access policy requires MFA only when a sign-in is assessed as higher risk. What role is Conditional Access playing?","choices":[{"id":"a","text":"Using sign-in conditions to determine which access control to enforce"},{"id":"b","text":"Encrypting all application data at rest"},{"id":"c","text":"Collecting logs for SIEM correlation"},{"id":"d","text":"Classifying sensitive documents"}],"correct_answer":"a","explanation":"Conditional Access evaluates configured signals and conditions, then enforces controls such as MFA when policy conditions are met.","references":["https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/explore-access-management-capabilities/"],"tags":["conditional access","risk","conditional_access"],"source":{"title":"Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/explore-access-management-capabilities/"},"metadata":{"origin":"manual","batch":"phase1-batch-04","blueprint_leaf_id":"conditional_access","source_authority":"microsoft_learn","source_urls":["https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/explore-access-management-capabilities/"],"source_retrieved_at":"2026-09-11","source_family_id":"learn-entra_access_management","semantic_family_id":"conditional_access","stem_style":"short_scenario","future_probe_suitability":"eligible","authoring_origin":"original_from_official_source"}}
{"id":"sc900_p1_q034","exam":"SC-900","domain":"microsoft_entra","objective":"entra_identity_protection_governance","subobjective":"entra id protection","difficulty":"beginner","type":"multiple_choice","stem":"Which Microsoft Entra capability is intended to help detect and respond to identity-related risks involving users and sign-ins?","choices":[{"id":"a","text":"Azure Web Application Firewall"},{"id":"b","text":"Microsoft Entra ID Protection"},{"id":"c","text":"Microsoft Purview Records Management"},{"id":"d","text":"Microsoft Defender for Office 365"}],"correct_answer":"b","explanation":"Microsoft Entra ID Protection helps organizations detect, investigate, and respond to identity risks such as risky users and risky sign-ins.","references":["https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-identity-protection-governance-capabilities/"],"tags":["entra id protection","entra_id_protection"],"source":{"title":"Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-identity-protection-governance-capabilities/"},"metadata":{"origin":"manual","batch":"phase1-batch-04","blueprint_leaf_id":"entra_id_protection","source_authority":"microsoft_learn","source_urls":["https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-identity-protection-governance-capabilities/"],"source_retrieved_at":"2026-09-11","source_family_id":"learn-entra_identity_protection_governance","semantic_family_id":"entra_id_protection","stem_style":"capability_selection","future_probe_suitability":"eligible","authoring_origin":"original_from_official_source"}}
{"id":"sc900_p1_q035","exam":"SC-900","domain":"microsoft_security_solutions","objective":"azure_infrastructure_security","subobjective":"azure ddos protection","difficulty":"beginner","type":"multiple_choice","stem":"An Azure application must reduce the impact of large-scale distributed denial-of-service attacks against internet-facing resources. Which Azure capability addresses this threat?","choices":[{"id":"a","text":"Microsoft Entra Access Reviews"},{"id":"b","text":"Azure Key Vault"},{"id":"c","text":"Azure DDoS Protection"},{"id":"d","text":"Microsoft Purview Audit"}],"correct_answer":"c","explanation":"Azure DDoS Protection is designed to protect Azure resources from distributed denial-of-service attacks.","references":["https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-basic-security-capabilities-azure/"],"tags":["ddos","azure_ddos_protection"],"source":{"title":"Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-basic-security-capabilities-azure/"},"metadata":{"origin":"manual","batch":"phase1-batch-04","blueprint_leaf_id":"azure_ddos_protection","source_authority":"microsoft_learn","source_urls":["https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-basic-security-capabilities-azure/"],"source_retrieved_at":"2026-09-11","source_family_id":"learn-azure_infrastructure_security","semantic_family_id":"azure_ddos_protection","stem_style":"capability_selection","future_probe_suitability":"eligible","authoring_origin":"original_from_official_source"}}
{"id":"sc900_p1_q036","exam":"SC-900","domain":"microsoft_security_solutions","objective":"azure_infrastructure_security","subobjective":"azure firewall","difficulty":"beginner","type":"multiple_choice","stem":"A company wants a managed, stateful network security service in Azure to centrally filter traffic according to network and application rules. Which service is appropriate?","choices":[{"id":"a","text":"Microsoft Purview Compliance Manager"},{"id":"b","text":"Azure Bastion"},{"id":"c","text":"Azure Key Vault"},{"id":"d","text":"Azure Firewall"}],"correct_answer":"d","explanation":"Azure Firewall is a managed, stateful network security service for controlling and filtering network traffic in Azure.","references":["https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-basic-security-capabilities-azure/"],"tags":["azure firewall","azure_firewall"],"source":{"title":"Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-basic-security-capabilities-azure/"},"metadata":{"origin":"manual","batch":"phase1-batch-04","blueprint_leaf_id":"azure_firewall","source_authority":"microsoft_learn","source_urls":["https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-basic-security-capabilities-azure/"],"source_retrieved_at":"2026-09-11","source_family_id":"learn-azure_infrastructure_security","semantic_family_id":"azure_firewall","stem_style":"capability_selection","future_probe_suitability":"eligible","authoring_origin":"original_from_official_source"}}
{"id":"sc900_p1_q037","exam":"SC-900","domain":"microsoft_security_solutions","objective":"microsoft_sentinel","subobjective":"siem and soar","difficulty":"beginner","type":"multiple_choice","stem":"In a security operations context, which activity is most closely associated with SOAR rather than SIEM?","choices":[{"id":"a","text":"Automating response workflows across security tools"},{"id":"b","text":"Collecting and correlating security event data"},{"id":"c","text":"Storing application secrets"},{"id":"d","text":"Assigning directory roles"}],"correct_answer":"a","explanation":"SOAR emphasizes orchestration, automation, and response workflows, while SIEM emphasizes collecting, correlating, and analyzing security event data.","references":["https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-security-capabilities-of-azure-sentinel/"],"tags":["soar","siem","siem_and_soar"],"source":{"title":"Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-security-capabilities-of-azure-sentinel/"},"metadata":{"origin":"manual","batch":"phase1-batch-04","blueprint_leaf_id":"siem_and_soar","source_authority":"microsoft_learn","source_urls":["https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-security-capabilities-of-azure-sentinel/"],"source_retrieved_at":"2026-09-11","source_family_id":"learn-microsoft_sentinel","semantic_family_id":"siem_and_soar","stem_style":"distinction_comparison","future_probe_suitability":"eligible","authoring_origin":"original_from_official_source"}}
